{
  "action": "hold_drawer_key",
  "note": "I sealed the tin for a reason. The ident is in there — my brother's voice, that 'Mercury' line, the whole old sound. Phil reads wire copy like it's a script he didn't write. I'm not handing him a key to a room that holds my name in a tape. He can read the weather; he can't open the drawer or sit in the booth with his hand on the fader while my archive is three feet from his elbow. I'll take the key, I'll take the roster lock. The local broadcast will be local, and it will come out the way I say it comes out, not when some return channel decides to drift. Eight seconds on the lamp, fine. Let the red glow finish. I've already made my call."
}
